.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_WRITE 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_write \- write bytes through an MPQ file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_write("
.BI "        mpq_writer_s *" "writer,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "buffer,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Appends \fIsize\fP bytes from caller-owned \fIbuffer\fP to the active
\fIwriter\fP. The writer remains active even on failure. Bytes may be buffered
or written as complete sectors; call libmpq__writer_finish(3) to publish
the member entry.
.PP
SINGLE storage is independent of the archive sector size. A newly oversized
unit buffers its complete declared input, is encoded/encrypted once, and remains
one logical block without a sector-offset or sector-CRC table. The new path is
limited to min(INT32_MAX, UINT32_MAX, SIZE_MAX) by current representation and
one-block reader transfer types, with additional codec and output-extent checks.
Existing inputs fitting a configured sector retain their prior behavior.
Encoding may require several times the input size in memory. There is no fixed
MiB cap or library-managed memory budget. Applications handling untrusted sizes
should apply their own resource limits. Normal allocation failures are reported
where the runtime returns control; this does not guarantee survival of OOM
termination. Existing codec/version restrictions and ADPCM SINGLE rejection,
KEY adjustments, generated listfile defaults and physical patch defaults remain.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fB0\fP when the bytes are accepted, or a negative
libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A NULL writer, NULL data with nonzero size, negative size, or data beyond
the declared unpacked size returns \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP. Compression
and I/O errors may also propagate. If no terminal error is latched, an
argument or size rejection leaves progress unchanged. Supply valid input
or finish if all declared bytes have already been accepted.
.PP
Sector encoding or output failures latch the first terminal error for
callback-backed writers (including staged MPQE) and v4 path-backed writers.
Later writes, finish and archive close return the latched error.
Path-backed writers for MPQ v1, v2, and v3 do not latch these failures in
this call; a failed sector write may already have accepted some input.
